pySMESH: Cartesian_3D with viscous layers refuses layer cells that fold over (SMESH V9_16_0;
applies after StdMeshers_Cartesian_VL_offset_error.patch).

Defect: where the solid offset by the layer thickness has surfaces closer together than the
grid spacing, the layer cells there are inverted, and the compute succeeds with them.

Symptom: a 2 x 2 x 2 block with a bore of radius 0.4 on its axis, layers on every face (3
layers, factor 1.2), grid spacing 0.25. At a total thickness of 0.2999 the offset bore comes
within 0.0002 of the offset walls. The compute succeeds: 57 of the 912 layer hexahedra are
inverted (BadOrientedVolume), the smallest cell volume is -7.8e-3, and the cells sum to 6.20
for a solid of 6.99. At 0.2995 (a gap of 0.001) and below, no cell is inverted.

Root cause: ViscousBuilder::MakeViscousLayers (StdMeshers_Cartesian_VL.cxx) joins each node of
the offset mesh boundary to its nearest point on the wall and divides that segment into the
layers, with no check of the cells it makes. Where the offset surfaces almost meet, the cut
cells of the offset mesh between them are degenerate, and the segments of the two sides cross,
so the layer cells fold over. The offset step itself succeeds (a valid solid), so
StdMeshers_Cartesian_VL_offset_error.patch does not see it. The layer builder is from SMESH
c9294ee68 (2022-06-17, "bos #17015 [CEA 17008] Body fitting with Viscous Layers for CFD
meshing"); upstream master at 83f8bf482 (2026-09-14) has the same code.

Change, in StdMeshers_Cartesian_VL.cxx only: after the layer cells of a solid are built and the
coincident nodes merged, MakeViscousLayers counts the layer volumes that SMDS_VolumeTool finds
not forward (as the BadOrientedVolume control does). If there are any, it clears the mesh, puts
"Viscous layers: N layer cells are inverted: the solid offset inward by the total thickness T
has surfaces closer together than the grid can follow, so the layers there fold over. Use a
smaller total thickness." on the shape and on every SOLID, and returns false.

Not changed: every mesh with no inverted layer cell, bit for bit; the layers in a face (the
two-step builder's 2-D path), which this check skips.

diff --git a/src/StdMeshers/StdMeshers_Cartesian_VL.cxx b/src/StdMeshers/StdMeshers_Cartesian_VL.cxx
--- a/src/StdMeshers/StdMeshers_Cartesian_VL.cxx
+++ b/src/StdMeshers/StdMeshers_Cartesian_VL.cxx
@@ -27,6 +27,7 @@
 #include "StdMeshers_ViscousLayers.hxx"
 
 #include <SMDS_MeshGroup.hxx>
+#include <SMDS_VolumeTool.hxx>
 #include <SMESHDS_Mesh.hxx>
 #include <SMESHDS_SubMesh.hxx>
 #include <SMESH_Algo.hxx>
@@ -1476,6 +1477,37 @@
   editor.MergeNodes( nodesToMerge );
   if ( isCanceled() ) return false; // pySMESH: canceled
 
+  // pySMESH: where the offset surfaces are closer together than the grid can follow, the
+  // layer cells there fold over, and the compute succeeded with them. Refuse the layers,
+  // leave no cell behind, and put the error on every SOLID, as for a bad offset mesh.
+  if ( !isMainShape2D )
+  {
+    int nbInverted = 0;
+    SMDS_VolumeTool volTool;
+    for ( SMDS_ElemIteratorPtr it = initMDS->elementsIterator( SMDSAbs_Volume ); it->more(); )
+    {
+      const SMDS_MeshElement* el = it->next();
+      if ( el->isMarked() && volTool.Set( el ) && !volTool.IsForward() )
+        ++nbInverted;
+    }
+    if ( nbInverted > 0 )
+    {
+      initMDS->ClearMesh();
+      const std::string text = SMESH_Comment( "Viscous layers: " ) << nbInverted
+        << " layer cells are inverted: the solid offset inward by the total thickness "
+        << _hyp->GetTotalThickness() << " has surfaces closer together than the grid "
+        "can follow, so the layers there fold over. Use a smaller total thickness.";
+      std::vector< TopoDS_Shape > failed( 1, theShape );
+      for ( TopExp_Explorer soExp( theShape, TopAbs_SOLID ); soExp.More(); soExp.Next() )
+        if ( !soExp.Current().IsSame( theShape ))
+          failed.push_back( soExp.Current() );
+      for ( const TopoDS_Shape& s : failed )
+        if ( SMESH_subMesh * sm = theMesh.GetSubMesh( s ))
+          sm->GetComputeError() = SMESH_ComputeError::New( COMPERR_ALGO_FAILED, text );
+      return false;
+    }
+  }
+
   // create a group
   if ( !_hyp->GetGroupName().empty() )
   {
